{#
    Where a screen of the import says what the last answer did (docs/features/data-import/pairing-screens.md "Answers
    in place"): it stays in view at the bottom of the screen - on a phone above the thumb - instead of a line at the
    top of the page. Fixed to the bottom of the window (a sticky line left with the list at the page's end, and
    "Undo the last one" with it); the script keeps that much room free under the page. Empty until an answer is given; an answer shown in place fills it
    (_answer_said_message.html.twig). It is announced to a screen reader when it changes.

    Variables: said (null, or what _answer_said_message.html.twig takes).
#}
<div id="import-answer-said" style="position: fixed; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px); z-index: 25; max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 12px; pointer-events: none;" aria-live="polite" data-testid="import-answer-said">
    {%- if said is not null %}{{ include('data_import/_answer_said_message.html.twig', {said: said}, with_context = false) }}{% endif -%}
</div>
